{"content_hash": "b37fd217d0666d22", "version_id": 669, "article_id": 67, "level_code": "ja_n2", "lang": "ja", "level": 4, "level_label": "N2 中高級", "title": "バンク・オブ・アメリカ、マネーロンダリング対策の不備で12億ドル超の制裁金", "title_zh": "美国银行因反洗钱不力被罚12亿美元", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "guardian_business", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/14/bank-of-america-fined-money-laundering", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1527874594978-ee4f8a05b4c1?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8YmFuayUyMGFtZXJpY2ElMjBmaW5lZHxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkyMDIyNTY4fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Melinda Gimpel on Unsplash", "author": "Melinda Gimpel", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@melindagimpel?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/petition-to-file-for-bankruptcy-9j8k3l9afkc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(122, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(160, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "04b2441ba82d"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-15", "word_count": 270, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "アメリカの金融大手バンク・オブ・アメリカは、疑わしい取引の報告を怠ったとして、アメリカの規制当局から12億1000万ドルの制裁金を科されました。同行は、この罰金が第3四半期の利益を押し下げると述べています。", "lead_zh": "美国金融巨头美国银行因未报告可疑交易，被美国监管机构处以12.1亿美元罚款。该行表示，这笔罚款将拉低第三季度利润。", "preview": "アメリカ財務省によると、この制裁金は同省の歴史で3番目に大きく、同行が50億ドルを超える疑わしい活動を政府に報告しなかったことが理由です。その中には、国家安全保障に関わるリスクがあるとされた10億ドルも含まれます。財務省のスコット・ベッセント長官は声明で、「この規模の銀行がマネー", "preview_zh": "美国财政部表示，这笔罚款是该部历史上第三大罚款，原因是该行未向政府报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动，其中10亿美元被认为涉及国家安全风险。财政部长斯科特·贝森特在声明中说：“像这样规模的银行如果未能履行反洗钱和制裁义务，后果将远超该行自身，使整个美国金融体系面临重大非法金融风险。”", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 657, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/ja_n2.mp3", "duration": 49.2, "size_bytes": 294624, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "jf_alpha", "word_count": 168, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@db9d57c/content/data/versions/669.json", "paragraphs": ["アメリカ財務省によると、この制裁金は同省の歴史で3番目に大きく、同行が50億ドルを超える疑わしい活動を政府に報告しなかったことが理由です。その中には、国家安全保障に関わるリスクがあるとされた10億ドルも含まれます。財務省のスコット・ベッセント長官は声明で、「この規模の銀行がマネーロンダリング対策や制裁の義務を果たさない場合、影響は同行にとどまらず、アメリカの金融システム全体に重大なリスクをもたらす」と述べました。", "財務省は、同行がコンプライアンス体制の構築において「収益を優先」し、自社の内部管理ではなく、法執行機関や他の金融機関からの照会に過度に依存していたと指摘しました。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["美国财政部表示，这笔罚款是该部历史上第三大罚款，原因是该行未向政府报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动，其中10亿美元被认为涉及国家安全风险。财政部长斯科特·贝森特在声明中说：“像这样规模的银行如果未能履行反洗钱和制裁义务，后果将远超该行自身，使整个美国金融体系面临重大非法金融风险。”", "财政部指出，该行在构建合规体系时“优先考虑收入”，过度依赖执法机构和其他金融机构的询问，而非自身的内部控制。根据同意令，该行必须聘请独立第三方审查过去的交易，找出当时未发现的可疑活动，并向财政部的金融犯罪执法网络报告。"], "body": "アメリカ財務省によると、この制裁金は同省の歴史で3番目に大きく、同行が50億ドルを超える疑わしい活動を政府に報告しなかったことが理由です。その中には、国家安全保障に関わるリスクがあるとされた10億ドルも含まれます。財務省のスコット・ベッセント長官は声明で、「この規模の銀行がマネーロンダリング対策や制裁の義務を果たさない場合、影響は同行にとどまらず、アメリカの金融システム全体に重大なリスクをもたらす」と述べました。\n\n財務省は、同行がコンプライアンス体制の構築において「収益を優先」し、自社の内部管理ではなく、法執行機関や他の金融機関からの照会に過度に依存していたと指摘しました。", "body_zh": "美国财政部表示，这笔罚款是该部历史上第三大罚款，原因是该行未向政府报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动，其中10亿美元被认为涉及国家安全风险。财政部长斯科特·贝森特在声明中说：“像这样规模的银行如果未能履行反洗钱和制裁义务，后果将远超该行自身，使整个美国金融体系面临重大非法金融风险。”\n\n财政部指出，该行在构建合规体系时“优先考虑收入”，过度依赖执法机构和其他金融机构的询问，而非自身的内部控制。根据同意令，该行必须聘请独立第三方审查过去的交易，找出当时未发现的可疑活动，并向财政部的金融犯罪执法网络报告。", "text": "アメリカ財務省によると、この制裁金は同省の歴史で3番目に大きく、同行が50億ドルを超える疑わしい活動を政府に報告しなかったことが理由です。その中には、国家安全保障に関わるリスクがあるとされた10億ドルも含まれます。財務省のスコット・ベッセント長官は声明で、「この規模の銀行がマネーロンダリング対策や制裁の義務を果たさない場合、影響は同行にとどまらず、アメリカの金融システム全体に重大なリスクをもたらす」と述べました。 財務省は、同行がコンプライアンス体制の構築において「収益を優先」し、自社の内部管理ではなく、法執行機関や他の金融機関からの照会に過度に依存していたと指摘しました。", "vocab": [{"word": "制裁金", "pos": "noun", "zh": "罚款", "note": "指因违反法规而支付的罚金。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "マネーロンダリング", "pos": "noun", "zh": "洗钱", "note": "外来语，指将非法资金合法化的行为。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "疑わしい", "pos": "adj", "zh": "可疑的", "note": "常用来形容交易或活动。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "報告", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "报告", "note": "此处指必须向当局提交报告。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "規制当局", "pos": "noun", "zh": "监管机构", "note": "指负责监督金融等行业的政府机关。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "財務省", "pos": "noun", "zh": "财政部", "note": "美国联邦政府的财政部门。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "コンプライアンス", "pos": "noun", "zh": "合规", "note": "指遵守法律法规和内部规章。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "同意命令", "pos": "noun", "zh": "同意令", "note": "监管机构与金融机构达成的和解协议。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "内部管理", "pos": "noun", "zh": "内部控制", "note": "指企业内部的监督和管理机制。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "金融犯罪取締ネットワーク", "pos": "noun", "zh": "金融犯罪执法网络", "note": "美国财政部下属机构，负责打击金融犯罪。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "民事罰", "pos": "noun", "zh": "民事罚款", "note": "与刑事处罚相对，通常由监管机构处以。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "停止命令", "pos": "noun", "zh": "停止令", "note": "监管机构要求企业停止违规行为的命令。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "外国資産管理室", "pos": "noun", "zh": "外国资产控制办公室", "note": "美国财政部下属机构，负责执行经济制裁。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "制裁プログラム", "pos": "noun", "zh": "制裁计划", "note": "指针对特定国家或实体的制裁措施。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Bank of America fined $1.2bn for money-laundering failures", "summary_original": "Third-largest fine in US treasury’s history, due to failure to report suspicious activity, may affect third-quarter earnings\nBank of America\n(BAC.N), has been fined $1.21bn by US regulators for widespread failures to detect ‌potential money laundering and other illicit activity, a penalty the bank said will hurt third-quarter earnings.\nThe US treasury department said the fine, the third-largest in department history, is due to the bank’s failure to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity to the government, including $1bn that posed national security-related and other priority illicit finance risks.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Bank of America fined $1.2bn for money-laundering failures\nThird-largest fine in US treasury’s history, due to failure to report suspicious activity, may affect third-quarter earnings\nBank of America\n(BAC.N), has been fined $1.21bn by US regulators for widespread failures to detect ‌potential money laundering and other illicit activity, a penalty the bank said will hurt third-quarter earnings.\nThe US treasury department said the fine, the third-largest in department history, is due to the bank’s failure to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity to the government, including $1bn that posed national security-related and other priority illicit finance risks.\n“Financial institutions are on the ​front lines of protecting our economic and national security,” the treasury secretary, Scott Bessent, said in a statement. “When a bank of this size ​fails to meet its anti-money laundering and sanctions obligations, the consequences extend far beyond its own walls, exposing the ⁠entire US financial system to significant illicit finance risks.”\nThe treasury said the bank “prioritized its revenues” in building compliance programs, and overly relied on inquiries ​from outside parties such as law enforcement and other financial institutions instead of its own internal controls.\nThe consent order requires\nBank of America\nto hire an ​independent third party to review past transactions, identify suspicious activity that the bank failed to detect at the time and report those transactions to the treasury department’s Financial Crimes Enforcement Network.\n“Financial crime compliance is serious, and we are responsible for getting it right,” said a Bank of America spokesperson in a statement. “We have invested billions of dollars in technology and dedicated thousands of ​employees to combat financial crime, and our team is far along with and committed to completing the work required to address the issues raised ​by our regulators.”\nThe spokesperson added that the bank’s third-quarter results due for release on Wednesday would include a non-tax-deductible charge of $1.2bn, which will reduce quarterly net income ‌by approximately ⁠17 cents a share.\nAnalysts have estimated adjusted earnings per share of $1.10, according to mean estimates compiled by LSEG, but that excludes one-offs like this fine.\nShares were down 2.7% in after-hours trading after closing the day down 1.1%.\nThe penalty is likely to add to negative investor sentiment and raise concerns about higher expenses and whether Bank of America can maintain its roughly $6bn quarterly share buyback pace, the UBS analyst Erika Najarian said in a note.\nWith earnings due ​on Wednesday, “we think shares likely underperforming at ​open”, she said.\nShe noted there ⁠was no asset cap, a regulatory penalty that would limit how large the bank could grow.\nAs part of the fine, the treasury department’s office of the comptroller of the currency levied a $750m civil ​penalty against the lender, the largest ever for the regulator, citing failures to address shortcomings in its anti-money ​laundering programs that were ⁠identified as part of a 2024 cease-and-desist order from the watchdog.\nThe regulator said the bank’s compliance program was “deficient and ineffective”, and its transaction monitoring system caused the bank to delay filing suspicious activity reports on billions of dollars of transactions.\nIn addition, the bank paid an $11.6m fine to the treasury department’s office of foreign ⁠assets control ​for more than 400 apparent violations of numerous sanctions programs. The treasury said the bank mistakenly ​processed millions of dollars in payments that violated sanctions programs targeting countries including Russia and Iran.\nThe fine comes days after American Express\nwas also hit with a $350m penalty\nfor similar anti-money ​laundering shortcomings.\nExplore more on these topics\nBank of America\nBanking\nRegulators\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-15T00:02:46.794735", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "アメリカ", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.775, "sm": 275, "em": 775, "cs": 0, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "財務省", "s": 0.775, "e": 1.375, "sm": 775, "em": 1375, "cs": 4, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "に", "s": 1.375, "e": 1.5, "sm"